# A4 accuracy suite: the site values A4 adds to H0's (bench/slurm/h0/site.env holds the account,
# partition, H0_ROOT and the venv; run H0's setup_env.sh once). Plain KEY=${KEY:-default} lines:
# an environment variable of the same name overrides a value for one call.

# A python with agama (the galaxy ICs; H0's venv has none). E.g. a venv with `pip install agama`
# (agama asks to download GSL/Eigen on first build), or a conda env with agama.
A4_AGAMA_PY=${A4_AGAMA_PY:-CHANGE_ME}
# An Odisseo checkout with tools/a4_galaxy_ics.py (branch a4/verification-suite until merged) and
# tools/agama_generate_scm_disk_ic.py beside it.
A4_ODISSEO=${A4_ODISSEO:-CHANGE_ME}
# The partition for the IC job (CPU only: agama's sampling). HoreKa: cpuonly.
A4_CPU_PARTITION=${A4_CPU_PARTITION:-cpuonly}
# Where the ICs live: shared across runs (generate once, ~25 GB at the largest N).
A4_IC=${A4_IC:-${H0_ROOT:-CHANGE_ME}/a4/ics}
# Baselines to check every rung against (<A4_BASELINES>/<tier>/<ladder>/<rung>.json), or empty.
A4_BASELINES=${A4_BASELINES:-}
